Chapter: EffectRowVarSyntax
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Stage 1b probe (EffectRows.md section 3). Row-variable syntax in
 signatures: a lowercase identifier inside effect brackets is a row
 tail, alone ([e]) or after concrete effects ([Console, e]). In
 stage 1 rows are inert — this program must parse, type-check,
 compile, and run; stage 2 gives the variables meaning. The printer
 must round-trip these signatures through TEXT emission.

Section: Definitions

  apply-row : (Integer -> [e] Integer), Integer -> [e] Integer
  apply-row (f) (x) = f x

  logged-apply : (Integer -> [Console, e] Integer), Integer -> [Console, e] Integer
  logged-apply (f) (x) = f x

  double : Integer -> Integer
  double (n) = n * 2

  shout : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  shout (n) = act
    print-line-uni ("shout " & show n)
    n * 2
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("pure " & show (apply-row double 21))
    r <- logged-apply shout 21
    print-line-uni ("logged " & show r)
  end
